All validations green — final review of the changes.
Root cause: `lib/context.js` set `ctx.assert = require('http-assert')`. `http-assert@1.5.0` depends on nested `http-errors@1.8.1`, while Koa `ctx.throw` and `Application.HttpError` use top-level `http-errors@2.0.1`. Errors from `ctx.assert(...,401,...)` were `UnauthorizedError` from the v1 copy, so `err instanceof Koa.HttpError` (v2 class) was `false`. App error middleware fell through to 500 `E_ASSERT_REGRESSION` instead of 401.

Files changed:
- `lib/context.js`: removed `http-assert` import, added local `ctxAssert(value,status,msg,opts)` using top-level `createError` (same instance as `ctx.throw`/`HttpError`), with `fail/equal/notEqual/ok/strictEqual/notStrictEqual/deepEqual/notDeepEqual` helpers mirroring `http-assert`. Strips `undefined` args (v2 throws on explicit `undefined`) and uses `deep-equal` with `util.isDeepStrictEqual` fallback.

Validation:
- Before: `bash /work/repro` → `ORIGINAL_FAILURE_REPRODUCED observed_http_status=500`.
- After: `bash /work/repro` → `ORIGINAL_FAILURE_ABSENT observed_http_status=401`.
- Manual check: `ctx.assert(false,401)` now `instanceof Koa.HttpError=true`, `isHttpError=true`; helpers also `instanceof=true`.
- `npm test` → 440 pass, 0 fail.

Remaining uncertainty: `deepEqual` uses hoisted `deep-equal@1.0.1` (loose) when present, else Node `isDeepStrictEqual` (strict) — loose edge cases (e.g. `1` vs `'1'`) could diverge on fresh installs. `http-assert` left in `package.json` unused; lockfile not updated.

